16. the 同用 grouping is DECLARED to callers that compare channels, not only used inside rhymes()
  PASS  the table answers as a partition over the 韻, not only over a character
          `rhyme_keys` takes a CHARACTER and reads (韻, 聲); a channel comparison holds the 韻 alone and had no way to ask for the grouping. quality/relations.py's 'Middle Chinese end rhyme (同用 group)' therefore compared 尤 with 侯 at the IDENTITY and read 流/樓 -- the pair the whole grouping exists for -- as False, while this module read True. The table was never wrong; nothing handed it over.
  PASS  a 韻 the grouping does not list is its own group, which can only make a checker stricter
  PASS  the declaration says which quotients it authorises
  PASS  ...and 'qieyun' authorises NONE, because that is what the coordinate means
          the raw rime class is finer than any poet used and 流/樓 is False under it (section 2) -- a schema NAMED for the 同用 group has nothing to ask for there, and refusing is not the same answer as False (doctrine 79).
  PASS  ...and neither does 'cilin', because its 部 is not a function of the 韻 alone
          詞林正韻 merges 上 with 去 inside a 部 and holds the five 入聲 部 apart, so 冬 is 第1部 in 平上去 and 第15部 in 入. A 韻-keyed quotient would merge exactly the cells this standard separates; `rhyme_keys` reads (韻, 聲) and is the method that can answer it.
  PASS  the tone-invariant partition agrees with the SOURCED 平水 table on 1,649 of 1,653 韻-pairs, and the 4 exceptions are named
          1649/1653. The four are 嚴/添 and 嚴/鹽 (the 入聲 業 split section 3 pins), 眞/臻, and 祭/齊. The relation layer's second channel is `prominence`, which carries the 平/仄 binary, so 上, 去 and 入 are ONE value there and a tone-split partition could not be expressed at that layer even if it were handed over. The grain is stated rather than assumed, and this is the number it costs.
